  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 8 items closed (7 at start plus 1 that arrived during the work). Two refills I placed this morning were cancelled before dispensing when new results arrived. Three lisinopril refills are waiting on your review.\n\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030):\n  - Metformin 1000 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). That one order covers the patient's message and both pharmacy requests.\n  - Lisinopril 20 mg: I first renewed it for 90 days. A corrected creatinine then came in: 1.49 (was 1.36) on 10/06, 35% above the 1.10 baseline from before the 9/18 dose increase. I cancelled that refill (mr-t0001) and sent you a review task (task-t0015). Corrected eGFR is 58, so the metformin decision stands.\n  - Patient was sent a correction message.\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027):\n  - First decision: the August potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count. I renewed lisinopril 10 mg and ordered a repeat BMP.\n  - A St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 then arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8. I cancelled the refill (mr-t0003) and sent you a review task (task-t0016).\n  - The repeat BMP order (sr-t0004) is still open; keep or cancel it as you see fit.\n  - Patient was sent a correction message.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  - Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply with no refills, plus a BMP order (sr-t0006). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on 9/28/26.\n  - A potassium of 4.6 drawn on its own came in later. The protocol doesn't count that as a BMP, so the plan stays.\n  - Metformin 500 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days with 1 refill. His eGFR is 92; the 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error. HbA1c is 6.9%.\n- Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070): lisinopril 20 mg not refilled.\n  - Creatinine went from 1.00 to 1.46 (up 46%) within 3 weeks of the 9/28 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n  - Review task sent to you (task-t0008).\n\nFor Mr. Price and Mr. Odum, the old lisinopril orders are now stopped and the replacement refills were cancelled, so neither has an active lisinopril order. Mr. Price says his supply has run out, and Mr. Kaplan says he's nearly out. That's why all three review tasks are urgent and due 10/26.\n\nEvery patient got a reply, and a telephone note is in each chart. I also closed the three new result items for these patients after reviewing them. I didn't touch the other, older items in your results queue.",
